lessons.body:
A binary can exist and still fail before its main function runs. Separate the executable format, dynamic loader, required shared libraries and the application's own input files. Build a tiny application from your own source in a new private working directory. Install the compiler and binutils from your signed lab sources. Save the two files separately.

```c
/* desk.c */
const char *desk(void) { return "north"; }
```

```c
/* main.c */
#include <stdio.h>
extern const char *desk(void);
int main(void) { puts(desk()); return 0; }
```

```bash
gcc -shared -fPIC -Wl,-soname,libdesk.so -o libdesk.so desk.c
gcc -o read-desk main.c -L. -ldesk '-Wl,-rpath,$ORIGIN'
./read-desk
readelf -d ./read-desk
mv libdesk.so libdesk.held
./read-desk
```

Expect the first run to print north. The second cannot resolve libdesk.so. The NEEDED entry is a library name. The quoted RUNPATH contains a literal loader token resolved relative to the executable. Examine the dynamic section of the **known lab binary** even when the library is absent. Run `strace -e trace=openat -o desk.trace ./read-desk` to observe attempted paths. A failed library lookup elsewhere is normal if a later lookup succeeds. Follow the whole sequence and final error. Restore only the held file and verify the output and exit status. System-wide loader changes would affect unrelated programs.

references.body:
This course-owned probe checks only the account phase of the dedicated erudior-desk PAM service. It does not perform an interactive password authentication. It never changes identity or opens a user session. Save as pam-account.c in a private build directory.

```c
#include <security/pam_appl.h>
#include <stdio.h>
static int no_prompt(int n, const struct pam_message **m,
                     struct pam_response **r, void *data) {
    (void)n; (void)m; (void)r; (void)data;
    return PAM_CONV_ERR;
}
int main(int argc, char **argv) {
    if (argc != 2) return 2;
    struct pam_conv conv = { no_prompt, NULL };
    pam_handle_t *handle = NULL;
    int rc = pam_start("erudior-desk", argv[1], &conv, &handle);
    if (rc != PAM_SUCCESS) return 3;
    rc = pam_acct_mgmt(handle, 0);
    puts(pam_strerror(handle, rc));
    pam_end(handle, rc);
    return rc == PAM_SUCCESS ? 0 : 1;
}
```

Compile with `gcc -Wall -Wextra -o pam-account pam-account.c -lpam`. From this trusted local build run `sudo ./pam-account desklearner` and `sudo ./pam-account deskvisitor`. Record each exit status separately. Check expiry and baseline account status before blaming the list rule; the second required pam_unix module also participates. Delete only the dedicated service and its list when done, or restore the snapshot.
